{
 "annotations": {
  "destructiveHint": false,
  "idempotentHint": false,
  "openWorldHint": false,
  "readOnlyHint": false,
  "title": "Prepare a rikma for someone else"
 },
 "description": "Prepare a rikma on 1lev1 for ANOTHER person - not the user you are talking to - and get one link to give them: for example the user markets 1lev1 and sets up a new customer's business, or helps another member get started. NEVER use it for the user themselves; for their own business, partnership or idea use proposeRikmaBlueprint. If it is not clear who the rikma is for, ask before calling. Pass that other person's name and email as the user gave them for this, and the intent and blueprint exactly as prepareSignup takes them. If the person has no account yet you get signupUrl: they sign, choose a password and confirm their email themselves, then land on the prepared rikma (intent join/order also work here). If they already have an account you get receiveUrl (intent business/partnership/idea with a blueprint only): opened while signed in to the account with that email, it hands them the drafted rikma to review and create. Nothing is created until they do, and the user gets no access to it. Refused when the email is the user's own. The link is valid 14 days; previewUrl shows the draft to anyone with it. Docs: https://1lev1.com/mcp#prepareForSomeoneElseTool",
